    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--1\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">    甲伏怪是由底 棲魔魚改造後賦予智能的甲殼生物，也是底棲魔魚遠古帝國的殘存者。其腦中仍根深蒂固的保留着創造者的指令，而它們從古至今都嚴格遵循這些指令行事。</p></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">    <em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>太古遺存者</strong></em><strong> </strong><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>Primeval Relics。</strong></em>太古時期的底棲魔魚曾統治着橫跨數個大洋的龐大帝國，並用其強大的魔法扭曲凡間新生生物的心智。然而，底棲魔魚的水生習性使其必須依靠僕從，才能將其意志施加到水面之外。正是因此它們才創造了甲伏怪。</p></div><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">    完美服從的甲伏怪遵照底 棲魔魚的命令四處蒐集智慧生物與魔法。隨着世代的更迭，被設計有超強適應力的甲伏怪們變得越來越強大。而底 棲魔魚帝國隨着衆神崛起而分崩離析後，甲伏怪們也四散飄零。但它們仍然繼續做着曾經爲底棲魔魚所做的事務，仍在悠然的採集類人生物，積攢財寶，蒐集魔法，增強力量。</p></div><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">    <em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>不倦的守衛Tirelsee</strong></em><strong> </strong><em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>Guardians。</strong></em>甲伏怪仍守衛着底 棲魔魚帝國的遺蹟，沉默地遵從無數世代前的命令。有時，尋寶者們會根據流言和古代地圖找到這些遺蹟的位置，但膽大與無畏也只能爲其帶來死亡作爲獎賞。</p></div><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">    尋寶者死後，它們隨身的財物也將 歸入甲伏怪守護的寶藏中。甲伏怪可以在遠距離探知魔法。這種知覺與它們的本能會驅使其殺死探險者，並取走裝備財物，再埋在底棲魔魚指示的祕密地點。</p></div><div class=\"rd__b  rd__b--2\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN:left;MARGIN:0pt;mso-pagination:widow-orphan\">     <em style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><strong>靜候的僕從Waiting Servant。</strong></em>雖然底棲魔魚的古代帝國已經隕落多時，但它們 與甲伏怪的心靈聯結依然完好無損。接觸到底棲魔魚的甲伏怪會立刻恢復其舊時的角色，重拾爲底棲魔魚邪惡意圖服務的強烈衝動。</p></div></div><p>Survivors of the ancient aboleth empire, chuuls are crustaceans the aboleths modified and endowed with sentience. They follow the ingrained directives of their creators, as they have done since the dawn of time.</p><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Primeval Relics\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Primeval Relics.</span> In the primeval ages, aboleths ruled a vast empire that spanned the oceans of the world. In those days, the aboleths used mighty magic and bent the minds of the nascent creatures of the mortal realm. However, they were bound to the water and could not enforce their will beyond it without servants. Therefore, they created chuuls.</p><p>Perfectly obedient, the chuuls collected sentient creatures and magic at the aboleths' command. Chuuls were designed to endure the ages of the world, growing in size and strength as the eons passed. When the aboleths' empire crumbled with the rise of the gods, the chuuls were cast adrift. However, these creatures continue to do what they did for the aboleths, slowly collecting humanoids, gathering treasure, amassing magic, and consolidating power.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Tireless Guardians\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Tireless Guardians.</span> Chuul still guard the ruins of the ancient aboleth empire. They linger in silent observance of eons-old commands. Rumors and ancient maps sometimes lure treasure seekers to these ruins, but the reward for their boldness is death.</p><p>Whatever riches that the explorers bring with them adds to the hoard guarded by the chuuls. Chuuls can sense magic at a distance. This sense couples with an innate drive that leads them to slay explorers, take their gear, and bury it in secret locales aboleths dictated eons ago.</p></div><div data-roll-name-ancestor=\"Waiting Servants\" class=\"rd__b  rd__b--3\"><p><span class=\"entry-title-inner\">Waiting Servants.</span> Although the aboleths' ancient empire fell long ago, the psychic bonds between them and their created servants remain intact. Chuuls that come into contact with aboleths immediately assume their old roles. Such chuuls redirect their compulsions to the service of the aboleths' sinister purposes.</p></div></div></div>",
